1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
Your AI wrote the feature, wrote the tests, and shipped it.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:12,000
One endpoint changed. Three others broke. Nothing in the suite noticed.

3
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:16,500
AI could only imagine a handful of people using this.

4
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:20,000
Someone has to cover the rest.

5
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:27,000
So Keploy studies the traffic you already have, and works out who else shows up.

6
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:32,500
Keploy sits between your app and everything your app calls.

7
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:38,000
Then Keploy turns that into the ordinary cases, and the awkward ones.

8
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:42,500
Keploy runs every one again, against the recordings.

9
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:49,000
Keploy hands back passes and failures together, so nothing slips through.

10
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:52,000
Find it here, not in production.

